          {
            "commit": "39114fbe812ba1b4ae1fa01521769b78f4b42070",
            "subject": "LU-6132 o2iblnd: fix races with the failover thread"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Chris Horn",
          "email": "chorn@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-10-09 15:39:53.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Chris Horn",
          "email": "chorn@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-10-13 19:53:33.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-6132 o2iblnd: release and rebuild an HCA on device removal",
        "message": "LU-6132 o2iblnd: release and rebuild an HCA on device removal\n\nA VF reset or \"rdma link delete\" with LNet up blocks the device\nunregister in cma_process_remove(). The o2iblnd CM handler ignores\nDEVICE_REMOVAL, and rdma_cm sends no DISCONNECTED after it. So each\nconn keeps its CM ref and its cm_id.\n\nRegister an ib_client. The RDMA core calls its remove() before\nrdma_cm sends DEVICE_REMOVAL, because ko2iblnd registers after\nrdma_cm. Its remove() makes the NI fatal and closes the conns on the\ndevice. It drops each CM ref, because a dead device can fail the\nDREQ with no CM event. It returns after the last conn and pool of\neach hdev on the device are gone. Then add() lets the failover\nthread build a new hdev, for any dev_failover value.\n\n    Soft-RoCE, 2 VMs, rdma link delete, then rdma link add\n    without the fix: delete blocked for more than 60 s\n    with the fix:    6 of 6 deletes in 1 s, lctl ping OK after add\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial nettype=o2ib testlist=sanity-lnet\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Ib0530e74ba712ad349c2faa7af9dde16b0d06d79\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
